# Experiment 3 (v3): Leak-Free Hyperspectral Band Selection & ViT-Graph Classification

A rigorous experimental benchmark for **Hyperspectral Image (HSI) Band Selection** and **Hybrid Vision Transformer + Superpixel Graph Classification** on the **Salinas** dataset (`512 × 217` pixels, `204` spectral bands, `54,129` labeled pixels across `16` agricultural classes).

This repository eliminates the **spatial and label leakage** present in standard random pixel splits (`v2`, where every method reached `~99.95%` OA) and evaluates whether differentiable band selection (`ConcreteSelector`) can match or outperform full-spectrum models under strict spatial disjointness (`SPLIT = "group"`).

---

## 1. The Problem

Hyperspectral sensors capture hundreds of contiguous narrowband channels that enable fine-grained material discrimination, but introduce **severe spectral redundancy**, higher storage/compute costs, and **overfitting** when labeled spatial regions are limited.

More critically, standard HSI classification benchmarks suffer from two forms of evaluation leakage:

1. **Patch Overlap & Superpixel Leakage:** Random pixel-level train/test splits place training and test pixels inside the same homogeneous crop fields. Extracting `7 × 7` spatial patches and building superpixel graphs causes training and test windows to overlap and share labeled graph nodes—artificially inflating Overall Accuracy (OA) to **~99.95%**.
2. **Misleading Band Ranking:** Under leaky splits, correlated adjacent bands appear interchangeable because nearby pixels share nearly identical spectra. Under true spatial separation, naive univariate filters (such as ANOVA F-tests) collapse onto clusters of adjacent, redundant bands and fail to generalize.

---

## 2. How We Solved It: Leak-Free Evaluation Protocol

To measure genuine out-of-region generalization, `v3` enforces a strict four-stage leak-free pipeline:

| Stage | Implementation (`SPLIT = "group"`, `GRAPH_SEG = "fixed"`) | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **1. Label-Free Superpixel Partitioning** | SLIC (`N_SEGMENTS = 200`, `COMPACTNESS = 0.1`) segments the first 3 standardized PCs of the scene into **`170` reference superpixels** shared across all methods. | Keeps region geometry fixed and label-free so accuracy differences reflect only the chosen bands. |
| **2. Class-Balanced Disjoint Split** | Whole superpixels are greedily assigned to test (`SPLIT_SEED = 42`), yielding **`20,414` test pixels (`37.7%`)** while guaranteeing every one of the `16` classes retains **$\ge 40\%$** of its pixels for training. | Prevents test pixels from sharing superpixel graph nodes with training labels without starving minority classes. |
| **3. Exact Patch-Radius Buffer** | A `13 × 13` morphological dilation (`2 × (PATCH - 1) + 1` for `PATCH = 7`) around test pixels removes **`12,775` boundary training pixels**, leaving **`20,940` training pixels**. | Guarantees **zero pixel overlap** even at the corners of training and test `7 × 7` windows. |
| **4. Train-Only Fitting & Noise Check** | `StandardScaler`, `PCA`, `f_classif`, and `ConcreteSelector` are fit exclusively on post-buffer `train_idx`. A 6-run sanity check (`MODE = "check"`) verified realistic variance (`88.21% ± 0.57%` PCA, `87.13% ± 1.14%` uniform at `k=10`) before launching the 60-run grid. | Eliminates statistical and feature-selection leakage from test pixels. |

