* **`learned` Peaks at `k = 5` and Declines at Larger Budgets (`k = 20, 40`):** `ConcreteSelector` optimizes a 1-pixel MLP proxy on an internal random pixel split (`93.1%–94.5%` held-out accuracy). At $k \in \{20, 40\}$, high selector capacity overfits intra-superpixel spectral quirks (`85.65%` at `k = 20`, `83.69%` at `k = 40`), compounded by `MIN_GAP = 3` blocking up to `120` of `204` bands during greedy discretization.
* **`PCA` Scales Monotonically (`87.56%` $\rightarrow$ `91.59%`):** Orthogonal compression removes collinear spectral noise that causes the uncompressed `204`-band model (`86.27%`) to overfit training superpixels, reaching **`91.33%`** at `k = 30` and **`91.59%`** at `k = 40`.
* **`ANOVA` Stalls Across All Budgets (`81.29%–82.49%`):** Univariate F-score ranking fails to improve even as $k$ increases from `5` to `40`, trailing `random` subsets (`85.83%` at `k = 5`) by more than **4.4%**.

